# The raw route registrations in gvisor-tap-vsock fca6da3418e8e6bd3b0f4f1a8c8bc1a2e84e2208
# -- the commit sandbox enforces egress with, not v0.8.9 -- as grepped.
#
# Not the assembled paths -- `upstream-routes.txt` is those, and assembling
# them means composing three nested muxes by hand. This is the input to that
# assembly, stored so a change to it can be NOTICED. If upstream registers a
# route, moves one, or renames a mount point, this file stops matching and
# someone re-does the assembly; without it `upstream-routes.txt` can go on
# being checked against a version it no longer describes.
#
# `/connect` is not here: upstream registers it from types.ConnectPath rather
# than a literal, so the constant is checked separately.
#
# Regenerate with scripts/upstream-snapshots.sh --write.
mux.Handle("/dhcp/"
mux.Handle("/dns/"
mux.Handle("/forwarder/"
mux.Handle("/services/"
mux.HandleFunc("."
mux.HandleFunc("/add"
mux.HandleFunc("/all"
mux.HandleFunc("/cam"
mux.HandleFunc("/expose"
mux.HandleFunc("/leases"
mux.HandleFunc("/stats"
mux.HandleFunc("/tunnel"
mux.HandleFunc("/unexpose"
